<title>FRANCE: MOTORCYCLING-CRIVILLE QUICKEST IN PRACTICE.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-CRIVILLE QUICKEST IN PRACTICE.</headline>
<dateline>LE CASTELLET, France 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alex Criville upstaged Honda team mate Michael Doohan in Friday's opening practice for the French motorcycling grand prix at Le Castellet.</p>
<p>Spaniard Criville was fastest on the 3.786-km track, clocking one minute 21.456 seconds. Doohan, the reigning world champion and world championship leader, was second fastest in 1:21.737.</p>
<p>&quot;I've beaten him once this season in the Spanish Grand Prix. I know I can do it again,&quot; said Criville.</p>
<p>Italian Doriano Romboni, on an Aprilia, clocked the third fastest time, 1:21.916, for Sunday's race.</p>
